{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"text":" is a domain plugin that owns a ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slice, fetches a JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a so reads are synchronous and offline-capable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three flag types from one wire format:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"boolean","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — on\/off with rollout percentage (0–100)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"variant"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — string-typed weighted variants for A\/B tests.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"value"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — typed remote-tunable scalar ("},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For end-to-end wiring, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","level":2,"text":"Library target"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}]},{"text":"Wire format","type":"heading","anchor":"Wire-format","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["{","  \"version\": 1,","  \"flags\": {","    \"new_onboarding\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"rollout\": 25 },","    \"checkout_layout\": {","      \"type\": \"variant\",","      \"variants\": [","        { \"value\": \"control\", \"weight\": 50 },","        { \"value\": \"treatment\", \"weight\": 50 }","      ]","    },","    \"max_free_uploads\": { \"type\": \"value\", \"value\": 5 }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin rejects unknown "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"text":" values and falls back to the last-known-good cache. Defaults always live in Swift at the call site — this keeps them type-checked and forces “what if missing?” thinking.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Bucketing and identity","type":"heading","anchor":"Bucketing-and-identity","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket = FNV1a(bucketingID + \":\" + flagKey) % 100"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable per "},{"code":"(bucketingID, flagKey)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pair forever."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Same input always produces the same bucket."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per-flag."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A user isn’t always in the “early” group across different flags."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identity resolution."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" When a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userIDKeyPath"},{"type":"text","text":" is configured "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the current user ID is non-nil, that is used. Otherwise the install ID is used. Anonymous users get a stable per-install identity; logged-in users get stable cross-device assignment. A user’s variant ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"can","type":"text"}]},{"text":" shift once at login — acceptable for nearly all real use cases.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FNV-1a was chosen because it’s simple, dependency-free, and matches GrowthBook’s algorithm so apps migrating from GrowthBook get compatible buckets."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Evaluation order","anchor":"Evaluation-order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For each read, in priority:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Local override present?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Return it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flag in remote config?"}]},{"text":" Evaluate (rollout \/ variant assignment \/ value lookup).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" return the Swift-side default."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Persistence","anchor":"Persistence"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Install ID"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" persisted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" on first generation. Read at hydration via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState.hydrated(from:defaultConfig:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Last-known config","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" persisted after every successful refresh. Hydrates as fallback before first network success."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Local overrides"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" persisted by default. Restart = clean state.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exposedKeys"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"text":" persisted. New session = fresh exposure events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Exposure tracking","anchor":"Exposure-tracking"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A\/B testing is only analytically valid if you know which users actually saw each variant — bucketing alone is insufficient because the code path branching on the flag might never execute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["store.send(.featureFlags(.recordExposure(key: \"checkout_layout\")))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or via the SwiftUI sugar:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["WizardView()","    .recordsExposure(of: .checkoutLayout, store: store, action: AppAction.featureFlags)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin dedupes per session and fires the optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"onExposure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" callback (passed at plugin init). Wire that callback to your analytics plugin to forward exposures as events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Refresh policy","type":"heading","anchor":"Refresh-policy","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum RefreshPolicy: Sendable {","    case manual                                      \/\/ every .refresh fetches","    case automatic(minInterval: TimeInterval)        \/\/ debounce; default 300s","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apps dispatch ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"App.scenePhase"},{"text":" transitions; the plugin’s debouncing makes this safe to call frequently. The plugin does not subscribe to ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIApplication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" notifications — wiring stays in the host app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Service protocol","anchor":"Service-protocol"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol FeatureFlagsService: Sendable {","    func fetch() async throws -> FeatureFlagsConfig","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One method. Caching, hydration, evaluation all live in the plugin.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Built-in: `HTTPFeatureFlagsService`","type":"heading","anchor":"Built-in-HTTPFeatureFlagsService","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSONDecoder"},{"text":". Apps host their JSON anywhere — static file on a CDN, Cloudflare Worker, their own server. Zero backend infrastructure required. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/"},{"text":" is a runnable shared Worker serving flags + killswitch for a whole portfolio from one URL (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET \/<appID>\/flags"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Third-party adapters (LaunchDarkly, GrowthBook, Statsig) conform to the same protocol without changing the plugin.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Typed flag keys","anchor":"Typed-flag-keys"},{"code":["public struct BoolFlag: Sendable, Hashable","public struct VariantFlag<Variant: RawRepresentable & Sendable> where Variant.RawValue == String","public struct ValueFlag<Value: Sendable>"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read API on "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["state.isEnabled(.newOnboarding, default: false)","state.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","state.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reads are pure synchronous functions. Per-property observation works as it does for any other state slice — views re-render only when the flag they read changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Action semantics (selected)","anchor":"Action-semantics-selected"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"refreshSucceeded(FeatureFlagsConfig, fetchedAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is dispatched on every "},{"code":".refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (including debounced refreshes that return an unchanged config). Consume config transitions by observing ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a value derived from it — not by mapping this action. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewa